USIU First-Year Companion
1. Project Overview

The USIU First-Year Companion is a simple web-based orientation and cost estimator tool for first-year students.
It helps students estimate weekly expenses (commuting, meals, personal costs) and provides a basic study plan.

The project demonstrates:

HTML, CSS, and JavaScript integration

Responsive design with light and dark themes

Basic interactivity and data handling in the browser

Dockerized deployment for portability

2. Deliverables

HTML repo link: Contains the base HTML structure (index.html)

CSS + Docker repo link: Contains styling (styles.css) and deployment files (Dockerfile, .dockerignore)

README: Included in repo

Screenshots: Included in design/ folder (wireframes and final screenshots)

3. How to Run the Project
Option A: Run locally

Clone this repository:

git clone https://github.com/npm-devpatel/usiu-first-year-companion.git
cd usiu-first-year-companion/public


Open index.html in a browser.

Option B: Run with Docker

Build the image:

docker build -t usiu-estimator .


Run the container:

docker run -d -p 8080:80 usiu-estimator


Open http://localhost:8080
 in a browser.

